Subject: engine: packed arrays: array literals of numbers and the arrays Array.of/Array.from build start packed (QJS_PACKED_ARRAYS)

What this does
  A literal whose elements are all numbers is built directly in the packed kind: one pass decides
  int32 or float64 (js_arr_packed_kind_of), one allocation of the elements' own size, and the values
  are stored in place, with no JSValue and no retained reference. A literal with a hole or a
  non-number takes the existing JSValue path unchanged.

  A constant template that is itself packed (a literal the bytecode pool holds) is copied as a byte
  pattern: one allocation and one memcpy of count * element size, and the result keeps the
  template's kind. The template is never written to.

  Array.of and Array.from on the default constructor start their result as the int32 kind, so the
  appends they do keep a run of numbers packed and the first other value unpacks it. A subclass or
  any other constructor's own result is left exactly as it is.

Why we need it
  A number literal is the most common array a benchmark builds, and until now every one of them
  allocated a JSValue array and then had to be packed afterwards, or stayed generic. Building it in
  the kind costs one allocation of the elements' size and no reference counting, and the constant
  template case is a memcpy.

Hazards
  The kind is decided before any element is stored, so a literal with a non-number never starts
  packed and never has to unpack. js_arr_packed_kind_of uses the same test as the packed store
  (js_arr_packed_num_int): an integral float64 in int32 range is an int, but -0 is not (it keeps its
  sign, so the literal is float64), and the int32 boundaries 2^31 and -2^31-1 are float64.
  A constant template is read only; the copy owns its storage.
  With the flag off none of this code exists: regvm_array_from_regs, regvm_array_from_const and the
  Array.of/Array.from starts are guarded by the flag and compile to the previous code.

Tests: .local/kit/packed1.js literal shapes ([1,2,3], [1,2.5], [1,"a"], [], [,1], [1,,3], [...a,4],
Array.from({length},fn), Array.from(a), Array.of(1,2,3), Array.of(1.5,2), new Array(3) filled, map,
filter and flatMap results, a literal stored over with a string, 40 pushed halves, and [-0], [0,-0],
[1,-0,2], [2**31], [-(2**31)], [2**31-1] with Object.is and 1/x on each element); the 230-file
torture set with QJS_PACKED_TEST=0 and 1; asan on packed1.js; the AOT unit for packed1 and the array
kit kernels.
